== Effects ==
* Allows Isaac to carry two [[pill]]s. Tapping the Drop button will cause a cycle through the two pills.
* Spawns a random pill.
* {{dlc|nr}} Changes all [[card]] and [[rune]] drops into pills.
* {{dlc|r}} Changes all [[card]] drops into pills. Existing runes will not be converted, but new runes will only appear through forced drops (such as from {{i|Mom's Ring}} or {{i|Clear Rune}}).

== Notes ==
* Any Tarot card or rune held when picking this item up will change into a pill.
** {{dlc+|anr}} {{p|Dice Shard}} counts as a card and will be converted.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc|r}} If playing as {{C|Jacob and Esau}}, if one character picks up Little Baggy while the other character holds a card, that card will remain until used or dropped.
* {{dlc|r}} Blowing up the [[Rocks#Marked Skulls|skull]] marked with a small "X" in {{s|Depths}} will drop [[Telepills]] instead of {{P|0 - The Fool}}.
** If The Fool has already been generated, the generated pill will not be guaranteed to be a Telepills.
* {{dlc|r}} [[Tainted Characters]] who have an active item in the consumable slot will be allowed a third slot for pills.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Blank Card}}: All cards are replaced by pills, rendering Blank Card useless unless Isaac also has {{i|Starter Deck}}.
* {{i|Crystal Ball}}: Generates pills instead of cards upon use.
* {{i|Deck of Cards}}: The item becomes functionally identical to {{I|Mom's Bottle of Pills}}.
** {{dlc|r}} During multiplayer, if Little Baggy is held by one player, other players can still spawn cards using Deck of Cards. Dropping the card will convert it into a pill.
* {{I|False PHD}}: Since all cards turn to pills, there is potential for a lot of damage ups.
* {{i|Lucky Foot|r}}: Most negative pills will be converted to their positive counterparts.
* {{i|PHD}}/{{i|Virgo}}: Most negative pills will be converted to their positive counterparts.
* {{dlc|nr}} {{i|Starter Deck}}: Overrides Little Baggy. Pills may still be for sale in shops, but dropping them turns them into cards.
** {{dlc|r}} Having both items allows both cards and pills to appear again.
*** Picking up Starter Deck while already holding Little Baggy will turn any held pills into cards.

